{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/398513-the-best-wod-modules-published","id":398513,"title":"The best WOD Modules published","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T00:05:29-08:00","id":398513,"title":"The best WOD Modules published","content":"So, which stories do you think are the best within each game? which ahve you run? how did they end up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T06:57:45-08:00","id":400276,"title":"","content":"Running the NWoD SAS <i>Fallen is Babylon</i> was one of my best storytelling experiences ever.<br /> <br /> I've also used some of the vignettes from <i>Giovanni Chronicles I: The Last Supper</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T07:42:41-08:00","id":400306,"title":"","content":"<b>Baptism By Fire</b> in the first and second edition rulebooks for <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> really set out what <b>Vampire</b> was about - it's an &quot;adventure&quot; with basically no action in which the characters interact socially. I ran through a number of the first edition adventures after that, and the one that stands out in <b>Annabelle's Party</b> from <b>The Succubus Club</b>, a mystery with some action that investigates a social embarrassment rather than a more normal crime like a murder. The real standout of the line is <b>Giovanni Chronicles IV: Nuova Malattia</b>, a single-book &quot;epilogue&quot; with new characters caught up in a crime drama across the entirety of the 20th century, which is easily separated from the first three books and run by itself. <b>Dust To Dust</b> would be a good look back at the setting from Baptism years later.<br /> <br /> <b>The Skinner</b> is a very solid addition to <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b> - it manages to make Samuel Haight a scary idea again.<br /> <br /> <b>Loom Of Fate</b> established how powerful <b>Mage: The Ascension</b> characters could be relative to their environment, and how strange that environment could become.<br /> <br /> The adventures in <b>Love Beyond Death</b> emphasised the importance of Passion and the chaos it can cause in <b>Wraith: The Oblivion</b>.<br /> <br /> The best run of adventures in the Classic World Of Darkness, for me, would be <b>Orpheus</b>. It's a solid series that takes a workable premise and runs in a completely different way, full of surprises and twists as it builds to a conclusion, while also having plenty of options to play it different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:38:57-08:00","id":412395,"title":"","content":"Were there ever any &quot;modules/adventures&quot; for Revised or V20? Something like Transylvania Chronicles but set solely in the modern age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T01:35:32-08:00","id":412558,"title":"","content":"Well... not really. The model of adventures for White Wolf is not exactly standard. They make elaborate books that detail the setting, the players and the possible ways the plot may unfold. There are a number of major stories that are meant for players to be played in Revised. The final part of the <b>Ventrue Chronicle</b> is in the modern age, <b>Gehenna</b> has a number of apocalyptic endings for the game, <b>The Red Sign</b> is all about avoiding the Vampiric curse and mucking with Mages while <b>Blood Treachery</b> is all out war between Tremere and OoH presented as a play. All the <b>X By Night</b> books are loaded with ideas and miniplots that can easily be turned into an evenings or a chronicle's entertainment. <b>Nights of Prophecy</b> is all about weird and strange things happening in the WoD to the vampires and how they cope with it and the stories within while metaplotty have the makings of a couple of chronicles.<br /> <br /> For their quality... well. I have to say it's very much dependant on how much you like metaplot and crossovers :P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:24:34-08:00","id":414576,"title":"","content":"I thought <b>Nights of Prophecy</b> was all about making unfortunate purchasers fling a book across the room upon reading?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:29:40-08:00","id":414579,"title":"","content":"Step away from the metaplot and noone will get hurt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:07:58-08:00","id":415513,"title":"","content":"I liked the early modules from 1e, such as Alien Hunger and Awakening: Diablerie Mexico, the rest are too mired in metaplot for me to enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T21:05:44-08:00","id":416116,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't MET have put out some pre-generated &quot;modules&quot; or adventures for the LARP stuff that could be converted to tabletop play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:21:57-08:00","id":416818,"title":"","content":"There are just a few currently:<br /> <br /> <b>The Masquerade</b> boxed set came with an adventure, &quot;Unto The Not So Gentle Night&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse/pub/1/White-Wolf/subcategory/1_356/White-Wolf-Magazine\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf Magazine</a> had some LARP adventures (as well as tabletop ones) and some of them are available at DriveThru.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/63660/City-in-the-Sand-Minds-Eye-Theatre\" target=\"_blank\">City In The Sand</a> is the only standalone SAS adventure for Mind's Eye Theatre, and it's for <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>.<br /> <br /> By Night Studios has adventures among its forthcoming plans - <a href=\"http://www.bynightstudios.com/shop/books/blood-and-betrayal-booster-pack/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood And Betrayal</a> ran at LA By Night in 2014 and is available for pre-order at present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T07:05:28-08:00","id":417500,"title":"","content":"<b>WoD: Hong Kong </b>&amp; <b>Vancouver: Dark Alliance</b>. <br /> <br /> Reading through <b>Skinners</b> it looks like it could be. See how it works when I run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T21:03:43-08:00","id":419787,"title":"","content":"Blood and Betrayal looks exactly like something I'd like to get, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:08:26-08:00","id":425801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/398513-the-best-wod-modules-published?p=415513#post415513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the early modules from 1e, such as Alien Hunger and Awakening: Diablerie Mexico, the rest are too mired in metaplot for me to enjoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should check out V20's Dust to Dust. It's not really a sequel to Ashes to Ashes but more something set in Gray in the present day, with the events of that book and the later chronicles that were spawned being a distant memory with no actual bearing on DtD's events. Hell the only vampires still living in Gary are Modius and Juggler who have become old and rather impotent relics of a bygone era.<br /> <br /> I ran back in the summer as an introduction to VtM for my sister and her friends. It's a short little thing but made for a solid enough intro for new players or a new group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T01:10:35-08:00","id":426273,"title":"","content":"<b>Giovanni Chronicles: Last Supper</b> (so part 1) is probably the best 'official' module I have ever directed. Specially when the players don't know much what is coming. Heck, one friend of mine directed it making the characters believe they were going to play other game (something hunter oriented), and used *other system* even (I think GURPS, this was a long time ago and I obviously was not part of the group, so I can't remember) well, and they were *blasted* when at the end of the first part they were turned and they realized they were in a Vampire game.<br /> <br /> In my own experience, we played it by night, by candle light, and very much thanks to it I actually got laid with one of my players. And they did not stop speaking about it for ages. So that's how good it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3320-cathakjordi","user":"CathakJordi","date":". 03-03-2015, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3320-cathakjordi","name":"CathakJordi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T22:00:27-07:00","id":448828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CathakJordi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/398513-the-best-wod-modules-published?p=426273#post426273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]Specially when the players don't know much what is coming. Heck, one friend of mine directed it making the characters believe they were going to play other game (something hunter oriented), and used *other system* even (I think GURPS, this was a long time ago and I obviously was not part of the group, so I can't remember) well, and they were *blasted* when at the end of the first part they were turned and they realized they were in a Vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div>A friend of mine did the same to me and our group of friends once, although it began as Call of Cthulhu. Very fond memories of that game and that gaming group.<br /> <br /> Marshall, my friend, you are missed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:01:01-07:00","id":449059,"title":"","content":"Yeah I love Last Supper and the VtR QS. If you're going to run a long term vampire chronicle you might as well start with the Embrace and move forward from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:05:36-07:00","id":456008,"title":"","content":"Gotta second the Giovanni Chronicles 1 and Transylvania Chronicles IV is well worth a try too, it gets pretty intense. We played the latter as a group of 5th and 6th gen Methuselahs and went toe-to-toe with a proper old-school 4th gen Nicktuku whilst trying to repair a failing nuclear facility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T11:31:48-07:00","id":457077,"title":"","content":"That nuclear scenario was where <i>Transylvania Chronicles</i> lost me. It was a bit too much toward the Vampions end of the spectrum (and I liked <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</i> when it came out!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}